AI-ASSISTED DEVELOPMENT

This project was developed with significant assistance from AI coding tools.
We believe in full transparency about our development process.

During development, multiple AI platforms were evaluated. The project initially
explored several tools before settling on Antigravity as the primary agentic
coding assistant. The following AI platforms and models contributed to code
generation, architecture design, documentation, research, and code review:

  * Antigravity (Google DeepMind) — Primary agentic coding assistant (Gemini
    models). Settled as the main development tool for its deep agentic workflow.
  * Claude (Anthropic) — Code generation, architecture design, documentation,
    and deep research.
  * Gemini (Google) — Code generation, research, and documentation.
  * Cursor (Cursor, Inc.) — AI-powered IDE used during early development phases.
  * GitHub Copilot (GitHub / Microsoft) — Code completion and inline suggestions.

Human engineers direct the architecture, review structural relationships,
validate consistency across the codebase, and make all final decisions.
AI-generated code is treated with the same scrutiny as third-party dependencies
and scanned for license compliance.

