The fluxrig binaries link third-party Go modules. Their licences are permissive
(Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD) with the exception noted below, and each module carries
its own licence text in its source distribution. `go list -m all` from the
repository root enumerates the complete set with versions.

Mozilla Public License 2.0:

  * github.com/hashicorp/golang-lru/v2       https://github.com/hashicorp/golang-lru
  * github.com/hashicorp/golang-lru/arc/v2   https://github.com/hashicorp/golang-lru

    Reached through the Bento stream processor. MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft:
    it permits distribution as part of a larger work under other terms, and
    requires that the covered source stay available. It is unmodified here, and
    the upstream repository above is the source.

    A build that does not need Bento excludes it entirely, and with it the only
    MPL-2.0 code in either binary:

        make build-lite        # or: go build -tags nobento ./cmd/fluxrig

    That build links 61 modules and every one of them is permissive. The tag
    applies to both the Rack and the Mixer.

